# One entry: a trait the kernel PUBLISHES and its consumers use from outside this repo. `ChainsTraitMethods`
# is exercised by `tests/` (not an analysed path). `trait.unused` reads "not analysed", not "dead": it is a
# MEASUREMENT gap at a package boundary, which is this ticket's own thesis pointed back at itself, and no
# edit inside `src/` can close it.
#
# `HandlesRunnerIo` had the same entry until popcorn-runner-rehome 03.
# - MEASURED (control A, PRR03 unit 2): on 011c15ca, with the same dependency set and command, PHPStan reported
#   no errors and this entry matched; on the candidate it was reported `ignore.unmatched`.
# - INFERRED (source reading, not measured): 011c15ca has no `ProcessSession`; the candidate's
#   `ProcessSession` (`use HandlesRunnerIo;`) makes the trait used and analysed inside `src/`, which is why
#   the entry stopped matching.
# The entry is removed, not widened.
#
# Everything else is gone. 38 → 21 (ticket 46) → 2 (ticket 50) → 1 (popcorn-runner-rehome 03), by fixing
# contracts, not by widening. A ratchet a feature can widen is not a ratchet.
parameters:
	ignoreErrors:
		-
			message: '#^Trait Rushing\\Popcorn\\Concerns\\ChainsTraitMethods is used zero times and is not analysed\.$#'
			identifier: trait.unused
			count: 1
			path: src/Concerns/ChainsTraitMethods.php
